  "id": "between-subjects-design",
  "term": "between-subjects design",
  "definition": "A between-subjects design is a research design for comparing differences between means where different participants are placed in different conditions or groups, rather than being measured across all conditions. It is contrasted with a within-subjects design, where the same participants contribute measures in multiple conditions.",
